WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.210
"Turmeric Supplements and Liver Toxicity"

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.600
Liver injury associated
with turmeric:

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.000
Ten cases from the Drug-Induced
Liver Injury Network

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.720
in the United States,
and there are others too,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.120
including three cases
reported in Australia

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.640
and a series reported to
the Italian Ministry of Health.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.080
Is turmeric really
a new hepatotoxic substance?

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.320
First of all, regardless of what
the titles of the papers say,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.160
these cases appear to be from
turmeric extract supplements,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.720
rather than turmeric the spice.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.000
It's like green tea
and green tea extract pills.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.240
Brewed green tea appears
to be completely safe

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:40.960
for the liver,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.600
but give people green
tea extract supplements,

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.160
and the livers of as many as
1 in 17 people becomes inflamed.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.120
So, we should consume
our green tea in beverage form,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.200
not pill form,
and similarly,

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.400
our turmeric in spice form
at culinary doses,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.320
not capsules,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.960
unless they contain
just a single ingredient:

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.240
whole spice turmeric,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.400
not curcumin,
not an extract,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.640
no other ingredients.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.240
While turmeric extract
supplements

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.480
have a relatively safe
side-effect profile

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.200
even at high doses,
there is an increasing number

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.840
of case reports linking them
to liver injury,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.480
especially when combined
with agents such as piperine,

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.560
a compound found
in black pepper.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.000
As we've covered before,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.000
compounds like piperine
are added to turmeric

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.960
to enhance the
bioavailability of curcumin,

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.280
potentially contributing
to its toxicity,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.680
as one reason curcumin may be so
safe is that it is poorly absorbed.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.960
As we have cautioned before,

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.040
piperine blocks
liver detox enzymes

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.120
that can make some substances
like curcumin more potent.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.440
And turmeric curcumin
supplement formulations

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.560
with high bioavailability,
such as nanoformulations

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.480
or those with added piperine,
have been less investigated.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.280
There is a mistaken assumption
that if a little is good,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.120
then more must be better.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.360
We'd never make
that assumption for drugs,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.480
so why is it made
for supplements?

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.800
In this case, more does not
necessarily mean better.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.520
A review of nearly a hundred
randomized controlled trials

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.200
of turmeric or
curcumin supplements

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.600
for nonalcoholic
fatty liver disease

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.000
found that they successfully
calmed liver inflammation.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.160
And guess
which worked better?

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.560
Low-dose supplements
worked about 10 times better

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.960
than high-dose ones.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:24.240
There are caveats, though,
even for whole food turmeric.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.560
As Dr. Greger
has covered before,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.720
people who have a tendency
to form kidney stones

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:29.600
should be careful

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.880
due to turmeric's relatively
high oxalate content.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.120
During a routine exam,
this unfortunate man

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.800
was found
to have kidney failure

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.880
due to his chronic
turmeric intake,

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.200
which led
to oxalate nephropathy,

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.840
where oxalate crystalizes
in our kidneys.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.080
That was after taking
only 2 grams

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.040
or 2/3 of a teaspoon
of turmeric every day

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.680
for two years.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.760
And taking
a few spoonfuls a day

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.760
of the actual spice itself

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.840
may indeed be enough
to cause liver injury,

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.480
as happened
to this pregnant woman.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.960
Dr. Greger recommends
only a quarter teaspoon a day

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.600
in his Daily Dozen.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.680
There's also been concern
about lead contamination

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.680
of the whole food spice.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.960
Lead chromate
has been used

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.920
to make turmeric appear
more yellow in Bangladesh,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.200
where much of turmeric sold in
the United States is imported from,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.520
leading to multiple recalls.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.400
The wonderful news is
food safety policies can work!

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.040
Since the original paper
of lead chromate contamination

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.880
in turmeric from Bangladesh,

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.560
the portion
of market turmeric samples

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.760
with detectable lead

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.280
went from about 50 percent
to zero.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.240
Unfortunately, there is still
more work to be done, though.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.360
In four South Asian countries
where more than 80 percent

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.600
of the world's turmeric
is produced,

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.480
14 percent of samples had
detectable lead above 2 ug/g.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.320
For context,
this is 20 times higher

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.240
than the U.S. Food
and Drug Administration's

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.080
maximum allowable level
for lead in candy.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.600
And some stores
sold turmeric

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.520
containing much higher levels
of lead

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.000
that would result
in projected blood lead levels

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.080
in children up to
10 times higher

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.080
than the U.S. Centers
for Disease Control's

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.400
threshold for concern.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.120
This is a reminder that just
because something is natural

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.960
doesn't mean
it can't cause harm.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.440
Turmeric dietary supplements
are big business,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.240
estimated to account
for $69 million in sales

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.400
in the United States alone.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.120
Though its popularity does help
put the recent spate

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.600
of liver toxicity
cases in context.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.920
More than 10 million people
in the United States

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.000
take turmeric
or curcumin supplements.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.160
So, that would be like
one case in a million.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.120
Some people may just be more
susceptible genetically—

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.280
7 of the 10 patients
in this case series

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:39.760
had a genetic variant
that's relatively rare

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.240
in the general population.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.960
Still, it's safer for
everyone to use the real thing

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.000
and not some extract
in some supplement.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.440
And please don't let anyone
inject turmeric or curcumin

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.050
into your veins.

